{
  "dn23:0.1": "Long Discourses 23 ",
  "dn23:0.2": "With Pāyāsi ",
  "dn23:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "dn23:1.2": "At one time Venerable Kassapa the Prince was wandering in the land of the Kosalans together with a large Saṅgha of five hundred mendicants when he arrived at a Kosalan citadel named Setavyā. ",
  "dn23:1.3": "He stayed in the rosewood grove to the north of Setavyā. ",
  "dn23:1.4": "Now at that time the chieftain Pāyāsi was living in Setavyā. It was a crown property given by King Pasenadi of Kosala, teeming with living creatures, full of hay, wood, water, and grain, a royal park endowed to a brahmin. ",
  "dn23:2.0": "1. On Pāyāsi ",
  "dn23:2.1": "Now at that time Pāyāsi had the following harmful misconception: ",
  "dn23:2.2": "“There is no afterlife. No beings are reborn spontaneously. There’s no fruit or result of good and bad deeds.” ",
  "dn23:2.3": "The brahmins and householders of Setavyā heard, ",
  "dn23:2.4": "“It seems the ascetic Kassapa the Prince—a disciple of the ascetic Gotama—is staying in the rosewood grove to the north of Setavyā. ",
  "dn23:2.5": "He has this good reputation: ",
  "dn23:2.6": "‘He is astute, competent, intelligent, learned, a brilliant speaker, eloquent, mature, a perfected one.’ ",
  "dn23:2.7": "It’s good to see such perfected ones.” ",
  "dn23:2.8": "Then, exiting Setavyā, they formed into companies and headed north to the grove. ",
  "dn23:3.1": "Now at that time the chieftain Pāyāsi had retired to the upper floor o